  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "17862076",
      "title": "The \"ng add\" Command",
      "lectureOrder": 741,
      "videoOrder": 681,
      "sourceHash": "a8cb4cabeed2d3c8e95f4175cfedb054b77a7628f95bd57aefde312518383131",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "Instructor: You might know Angular material.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "It's a third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "actually also maintained by parts of the Angular team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 10.8,
          "en": "but totally optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.8,
          "end": 12.57,
          "en": "It adds components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.57,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "So pre-built components to your Angular app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 18.15,
          "en": "which follow the material design spec.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.15,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "Material design is a design language invented by Google.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "It looks the way this page looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "Now you can check out components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "and see which components this offers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "And this is of course not the focus of of this module here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "but there you can get nice prebuilt components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "which you can then easily drop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 38.58,
          "en": "into your application to use them there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 40.35,
          "en": "Now if we click on get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "we see that we can run one simple command to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 46.683,
          "en": "add Angular material to our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 50.613,
          "en": "Now let's copy this command and give it a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.78,
          "end": 53.79,
          "en": "Let's head over to our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 57.09,
          "en": "and there I will run NG add at Angular slash material.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "And Angular material is not the only package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "which supports the NG ad command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "Every third party package can support it no matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "if it's built by the Angular team or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "And there are a lot of third party packages out there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "For example, Ionic, which do support it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "Now to support it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "these packages need to include certain configuration files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "in their package source code in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "And NG ad will look for these files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "and if it finds them, it is able to run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 87.36,
          "en": "Now these files, which these packages have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 89.88,
          "en": "include then tell NG ad what to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 93.39,
          "en": "and let's see what NG ad does with Angular material.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.39,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "Lets hit enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 95.423,
          "en": "And now you see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.423,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "as a first step it installs packages through npm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now this is not all it will do though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 104.00999999999999,
          "en": "but it's one part of what it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 106.59,
          "en": "It will install all packages you need to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "install to use Angular material.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.88,
          "en": "That's the Angular material package itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "but also some third party dependencies this package needs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 117.63,
          "en": "Then, some packages or some tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "might prompt you for certain choices you have to make.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 123.39,
          "en": "Not all, some have some default steps which they always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 123.39,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "execute here, for example, we can choose a default theme",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "with which we wanna start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "And here I'll go for deep purple and amber,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "we can here also choose if you want to use hammer js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "for gesture recognition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 141.02,
          "en": "and I will choose yes, also add browser animations with yes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.3,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "so that we have all these nice animations and hit enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.21,
          "en": "And now you'll see it again updates the package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.21,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "dot json file because it now installs more dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "And that's the interesting part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.24,
          "en": "It did not just install some packages so it's not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.24,
          "end": 158.94,
          "en": "just a replacement for NPM install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "It also updated some other files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "It updated the main.its file, the app module, angular json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "the index HTML file, and styled css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "So why don't we have a look at all these files to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.25,
          "en": "understand what NG ad did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.25,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "And let's start with main ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 179.1,
          "en": "In main ts, you see it added a import for hammer js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.1,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "which is a third party package that helps us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 184.833,
          "en": "with gesture detection and that is it actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "In the index html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "you see it included some Google fonts, the material icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 193.95,
          "en": "in the end and the Roboto font, which it uses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 193.95,
          "end": 195.963,
          "en": "So that is an adjustment it made there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "In the app module, if we have a look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 204.54,
          "en": "There it actually added the browser animations module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.54,
          "end": 206.07,
          "en": "from Angular animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 209.19,
          "en": "because some Angular material components use animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.19,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "and of course those animations should work in these styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 215.31,
          "en": "CSS file, you see it sets some default styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 219.19,
          "en": "for your website, like a default fund for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "and in Angular json, there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "Let's see what a changed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 228.39,
          "en": "There you see that, for example, under the build command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 228.39,
          "end": 233.28,
          "en": "It now also includes our theme styles so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 233.28,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "that our theme is picked up when we build for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "So that's the NG ad schematic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "Pretty useful for third party packages that support it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 246.54,
          "en": "because it does not just install dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.54,
          "end": 247.74,
          "en": "in package dot json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 247.74,
          "end": 250.05,
          "en": "it also does this, but not just.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.05,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "Instead, besides doing that, it also makes a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "of adjustments specified by the third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 259.71,
          "en": "that need to be made so that you can immediately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 259.71,
          "end": 262.86,
          "en": "start using this installed third party package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.86,
          "end": 266.76,
          "en": "Now, I did mention NG generate and NG update as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 268.89300000000003,
          "en": "What do these schematics do?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
